infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Persisted queries vs open inline + complexity scoring
  desc Can you constrain every client? That answer picks the defence.
  compares
    - label Persisted queries
      children
        - label Closes the whole inline surface
          desc Arbitrary client queries become impossible; every bomb blocked at the gate
        - label Needs registration, breaks ad-hoc tooling
          desc Postman, curl, devtools can't hit production
        - label Best when you own every client
          desc First-party apps you build and deploy
    - label Open inline + complexity scoring
      children
        - label Required for public, 3rd-party APIs
          desc GitHub, Shopify can't constrain unknown clients
        - label Per-query cost cap plus depth limit
          desc Reject over ~1000 units; depth 7-10, alias cap 20
        - label Defaults invite abuse
          desc Needs deliberate tuning, or it fails open
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
